# ---- ClipIt, free edition. Copy this file to .env:   cp .env.free.example .env   (never commit .env) ----
# Put comments on their own line, as here: nothing may follow a value on the same line.
#
# Three ways to run ClipIt without an AI bill. Setup A is switched on below. To use B or C instead, put a # in
# front of the Setup A lines and take the # off the lines of the one you want.
# The full explanation, with the trade-offs: FREE.md

# ================================================================ Setup A (switched on): all on this computer
# No account, no key, no limits. Needs the Ollama app (https://ollama.com/download) and one download, once:
#   ollama pull llama3.1:8b
# Check it any time with:   python -m studio.ai_check   (it also tries a stretch of Hindi and Hinglish)
CLIPIT_AI_PROVIDER=ollama
CLIPIT_AI_MODELS=llama3.1:8b
# Streams in Hindi or Hinglish: if the check says "Hindi and Hinglish: WEAK", try a larger model (about 8 GB, fits a
# 16 GB Mac with other heavy apps closed). Run   ollama pull gemma3:12b   and use this line instead of the one above:
# CLIPIT_AI_MODELS=gemma3:12b
# A model that can "think" (Qwen 3 and newer) is asked not to, which is much quicker. To let it think: CLIPIT_OLLAMA_THINK=1
# The language spoken in your videos: auto (default) finds it out for each video; hi if they are all Hindi or Hinglish.
# CLIPIT_LANGUAGE=auto

# On a laptop, work on one video at a time so the model and the video work do not fight over memory.
CLIPIT_JOB_WORKERS=1

# How much transcript the model reads in one go, in tokens. These defaults suit a 16 GB Mac. A bigger number
# reads more at once but needs more memory. ClipIt raises it by itself, up to the second number, for a long request.
# CLIPIT_OLLAMA_NUM_CTX=16384
# CLIPIT_OLLAMA_MAX_CTX=32768

# ================================================================ Setup B (switched off): free cloud plans in a chain
# The first service is asked first. When it runs out of free requests the next is asked at once, and so on.
# Your own computer goes last, so the chain can never run dry.
# Never add a card or turn on billing on these accounts: that is what keeps them free.
# Keys:  Gemini https://aistudio.google.com/apikey   Groq https://console.groq.com/keys   OpenRouter https://openrouter.ai/keys
# Model ids change often: use the ones each service lists today (OpenRouter's free ones end in :free).
# In the dashboard, Settings, AI, Find models lists the real ids.
# CLIPIT_AI_PROVIDER=gemini
# CLIPIT_AI_MODELS=PASTE-A-GEMINI-MODEL-ID
# CLIPIT_AI_KEY=PASTE-YOUR-GEMINI-KEY
# CLIPIT_AI_FALLBACKS=groq:PASTE-A-GROQ-MODEL-ID,openrouter:PASTE-A-FREE-MODEL-ID,ollama:llama3.1:8b
# CLIPIT_AI_KEY_GROQ=PASTE-YOUR-GROQ-KEY
# CLIPIT_AI_KEY_OPENROUTER=PASTE-YOUR-OPENROUTER-KEY
# If a service refuses a request as too long, or its free plan allows few tokens a minute, send less each time:
# CLIPIT_AI_WINDOW_MIN=6

# ================================================================ Setup C (switched off): no AI at all
# Put a # in front of the Setup A lines. Clips are then picked by loudness, and each gets a hook, a title and
# hashtags built from what was said and from the video's title.
